// Second player-authored `SpriteSummon` spell (written concurrently with,
// and unaware of, conjuration/the_folded_tower.ron -- see that file for the
// actual pilot). Prior NPC/monster usage this was cloned from:
// assets/common/abilities/custom/gigas_frost/icespike_targeted.ron. One
// non-spell player ability also predates both
// (assets/common/abilities/hammer/rampart.ron), but it actually wraps
// `SpriteSummon` inside `StaticAura`'s `sprite_info` field -- a different,
// aura-carrying path, not the bare variant used here.
//
// Real behavior confirmed by reading common/src/comp/ability.rs and
// common/src/states/sprite_summon.rs:
// - `SpriteSummon` has NO `energy_cost` field at all (unlike every other
//   spell variant) -- it was never designed to be player-cast-gated by
//   energy. The only throttle available is `meta.cooldown`, set below.
// - It carries no attack/effect/aura field whatsoever -- it can ONLY place
//   `sprite` instances in a radius around an anchor point. Any
//   blind/slow/damage rider has to come from the terrain sprite's own
//   physical properties (`SpriteKind::solid_height`,
//   common/src/terrain/sprite/mod.rs), not from a scripted effect. This
//   sheet's "blinding and slowing... mired" riders are dropped entirely --
//   no fitting primitive exists on this variant, unlike `StaticAura`
//   (which pairs a sprite with a real `AuraBuffConstructor`, see
//   plant_growth.ron/cacophonic_shield.ron in this folder).
// - `summon_distance`/`sparseness`/`angle` scatter sprites in a radial
//   wedge from the anchor (probabilistically, per-candidate-tile), not
//   along a straight line -- there is no "wall" or line-shaped placement
//   primitive. This is modeled as a dense (`sparseness: 0.25`, well below
//   rampart.ron's decorative 0.97 or plant_growth.ron's 0.55), narrow
//   (`angle: 90`) wedge of a genuinely solid sprite
//   (`SpriteKind::TallCactus`, `solid_height: 2.63` --
//   common/src/terrain/sprite/mod.rs) at the target point, reading as a
//   rough physical obstruction, not a literal unbroken 9 m wall (gaps will
//   exist between individually-placed sprites).
// - No sand-flavored solid sprite exists in the terrain catalogue.
//   `TallCactus` is the closest available desert-themed *solid* sprite
//   (most sand-adjacent sprites, e.g. `Mud`/small cacti, are either not
//   solid or too short to obstruct movement) -- a documented flavor
//   drift, same category as this batch's hardcoded-`DamageKind` notes.
//
// `anchor: Target` (not the default `Summoner`) so the wall forms at the
// chosen point within the sheet's 27 m range, matching
// icespike_targeted.ron's own targeted placement.
SpriteSummon(
    buildup_duration: 0.8,
    cast_duration: 0.6,
    recover_duration: 0.5,
    sprite: TallCactus,
    del_timeout: Some((58, 4)),
    summon_distance: (0, 3),
    sparseness: 0.25,
    angle: 90.0,
    anchor: Target,
    move_efficiency: 0.3,
    ori_modifier: 1.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane), cooldown: Some(24.0)),
)
